# CUBE IN BOWL — the recorded task, in sim.
#
# `language=` IS THE DATASET'S OWN STRING, byte for byte
# (`projects/so101-tower/datasets/cube-in-bowl/meta/tasks.parquet`,
# `tools/vla/smolvla_tasks_so101-tower_cube-in-bowl.tsv` token ids). A VLA
# conditioned on it in sim must see the same tokens it will see on the arm.
schema_version=1
task=so101_tower_cube_in_bowl
family=so101_tower
language=Grab the cube and put it in the bowl

# ⚠⚠ `Near`, NOT `In`. `In(brick, <region>)` would want a region attached to
# the BOWL's site, and the device region table bakes every site's world pose
# at the rest configuration (`gen_placement_tables.mojo` reads it off FK
# once; `region_move_joint` follows one SLIDE, not a free body). A region on
# a free bowl would be evaluated where the bowl PARKS. `Near` is body-to-body
# geometry and is exact on both paths.
#
# 0.045 IS THE GEOMETRY: a brick resting at the bowl's centre has its origin
# 0.018 above the bowl's (base 0.008 + half-height 0.0096) and up to ~0.03
# to the side inside a 0.052 inner radius — under 0.045. A brick standing
# AGAINST the bowl's outside is at least 0.062 + 0.016 = 0.078 away; one
# balanced on the rim at least 0.052. So the threshold separates "in" from
# every "beside" or "on top".
goal=Near(brick, bowl, 0.045)

active=tower
active=desk
active=bowl
active=brick

# THE REAL LAYOUTS: brick and bowl drawn over the printed-props recording's
# start poses, the bowl on EITHER side of the brick — the family's desk_brick /
# desk_bowl (24 Sep; before, desk_left / desk_right held 20/70 of the real
# bricks and 17/68 of the bowls). Sim rates before and after are not comparable.
#
# `:sep=0.135`: the bowl's centre stays 135 mm from the brick's — the recorded
# layouts' minimum (70 episodes); the radii alone allow 79 mm, and the expert
# grasped 1 of 14 draws under 100 mm (the bowl in the jaw's way).
init=bowl@desk_bowl:sep=0.135
init=brick@desk_brick:yaw
